{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "דם יהיה זובה בבשרה", :translit "dam yihyeh zovah b'visarah", :gloss "blood shall be her flow in her flesh"} {:he "הן דם נדה מטמא לח ויבש", :translit "hen dam niddah m'tamei lach v'yavesh", :gloss "behold, blood of a menstruant impurifies moist and dry"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "דם יהיה זובה בבשרה", :b "הן דם נדה מטמא לח ויבש"}], :frame {:text "The laws of menstrual impurity are detailed at Leviticus 15:19ff. The halakhic principle that impurity of a menstruant transfers whether by contact with moist or dry substances is rooted in tannaitic purity law; Maimonides codifies that menstrual blood conveys impurity in moist and dry states (Mishneh Torah, Hilkhot Metamei Mishkav u-Moshav 1:2, deriving from Mishnah Kelim 1:3). The Ba'al HaTurim compresses this into a gematria equating the verse's opening words with the halakhic formula.", :sources ["Leviticus 15:19" "Mishnah Kelim 1:3" "Maimonides, Mishneh Torah, Hilkhot Metamei Mishkav u-Moshav 1:2"]}} {:quotes [{:he "תהיה בנדתה", :translit "tihyeh b'nidatah", :gloss "she shall be in her separation"} {:he "עד שהיא תבא במים", :translit "ad she-hi tavo ba-mayim", :gloss "until she comes into water"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "תהיה בנדתה", :b "עד שהיא תבא במים"} {:kind :other, :note "He notes the equation works with letters counted against words (האותיות / התיבות)"}], :frame {:text "The verse states 'she shall be in her impurity seven days' (Leviticus 15:19), after which immersion in a mikveh is required for purification, as codified in Mishnah Mikva'ot and Maimonides, Mishneh Torah, Hilkhot Issurei Bi'ah chapter 8. The Ba'al HaTurim signals that this gematria requires an adjusted counting method—letters of one phrase against words of the other—rather than a straightforward letter-to-letter equation.", :sources ["Leviticus 15:19" "Mishnah Mikva'ot" "Maimonides, Mishneh Torah, Hilkhot Issurei Bi'ah 8"]}}], :arithmetic [{:a-value 603, :b-value 604, :len